# Changelog Rule

**Every time you make a meaningful change to this codebase, update `docs/CHANGELOG.md`.**

## When to add an entry
- New feature or page added
- Existing feature changed or redesigned
- Bug fixed
- Dependency added, removed, or updated
- Configuration changed (Vercel, Supabase, Next.js, Tailwind, etc.)
- Auth flow changed
- Design system token or component changed

## When NOT to add an entry
- Whitespace / formatting only
- Comment changes
- Renaming a variable with no behaviour change

## Format

Add a new `## [YYYY-MM-DD] — short title` section at the **top** of the changelog (below the header), newest first.

Use these subsection labels as needed:
- `### Added` — new files, features, components, routes
- `### Changed` — updates to existing behaviour or design
- `### Fixed` — bug fixes
- `### Removed` — deleted files or features

### Example entry

```markdown
## [2026-05-06] — Add leads table

### Added
- `app/(app)/leads/page.tsx` — leads list with search, sort, and filter
- `components/lead-table.tsx` — table component with skeleton loader
- Supabase migration `supabase/migrations/001_leads.sql`

### Changed
- Sidebar: added Leads nav item with `Users` icon
```

## Location
`docs/CHANGELOG.md` — always at the project root's `docs/` folder.
